# The static checks of our own C, Objective-C and C++ code (C-0010 section 3, C-0011
# section 2), for src/, tests/ and tools/ only; the forks under external/ keep their upstream
# configuration (C-0010 section 4). Every finding is an error. Each family below is on as a
# whole, and every check that is off says why:
#
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: C interfaces pass several values of one type, such
#   as the two readings of the memory stub; names and comments carry their order.
# - clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: it asks for the
#   bounds-checked functions of C11 Annex K, such as memcpy_s, which Apple's C library does
#   not provide.
# - misc-include-cleaner: it maps a symbol to the header that declares it, and Apple's SDK
#   declares many in internal headers, such as pthread_t in sys/_pthread/_pthread_t.h.
# - readability-identifier-length: tests use short names such as the loop index of a table.
# - readability-magic-numbers: the tests check documented values, such as the byte offsets
#   of the crash record, and the host names its own limits in macros.
#
# Two options narrow a check, each for the same kind of reason:
#
# - bugprone-sizeof-expression.WarnOnSizeOfPointerToAggregate: the layout table of the test
#   builds records the size of every member, pointers to structs among them.
# - readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: every check of the native tests
#   is a macro with a branch inside, which would count as complexity of the test.
#
# clang-tidy runs on the compile databases of the asan-ubsan and ios-device-test presets,
# which Apple's clang wrote; .github/workflows/ci.yml lists the run, and
# docs/design/native-host.md section 11 what to do when the pinned LLVM release disagrees
# with Apple's clang about a flag.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  concurrency-*,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers
CheckOptions:
  bugprone-sizeof-expression.WarnOnSizeOfPointerToAggregate: false
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: true
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(src|tests)/native/.*'
SystemHeaders: false
